% ============================================================================
% atmosphere-layers.query.adj — a worked recall over the earth-science
% atmosphere-layers library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what is the stratosphere
% known for?": it states no earth-science fact — it only `import`s the grounded
% table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the
% `atmosphere_layer_feature` rows and returns the feature + the table's
% source/locator/trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the
% feature `auroras`, recall the layer that has it — thermosphere). The `mantle`
% is a layer of the solid Earth, not of the atmosphere, so a recall on it
% abstains honestly — the engine never invents a feature.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli atmosphere-layers.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "atmosphere-layers.adj"

? atmosphere_layer_feature(troposphere, $Feature)    % expect weather
? atmosphere_layer_feature(stratosphere, $Feature)   % expect ozone_layer
? atmosphere_layer_feature(exosphere, $Feature)      % expect highest
? atmosphere_layer_feature($Layer, auroras)          % expect thermosphere — reverse recall
? atmosphere_layer_feature(mantle, $Feature)         % expect abstain — the mantle is a layer of the solid Earth, not the atmosphere
